From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_pr_fixes_use_quaran <>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:46:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] apps/examples: Add a test which trips the heap
 use-after-free detector

Nothing in the tree exercised the detector, so there was no way to tell
whether it reports on a given board, and no way to notice if it stopped
reporting.

Add an example which writes into freed heap memory in each of the
shapes the detector is meant to catch, and prints what should have
happened for each one:

  1. Write into a chunk still on the free list. Caught by DEBUG_MM_UAF
     on its own.
  2. Write to the first word of a freed block. Inside the free node
     bookkeeping, so it needs DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE, which covers the
     whole payload of a held chunk.
  3. Write after another allocation has taken the block. Needs
     DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE; without it the address already belongs to the
     new owner.
  4. Free the same block twice.
  5. Ordinary allocation traffic, which must stay silent.

Case 5 is the one that matters most: a detector which reports on
correct code is worse than no detector, so any output during that case
is a failure. Cases 2 and 3 print a different expectation depending on
whether the quarantine is configured, so the same binary documents
what each option buys.

The test corrupts the heap deliberately and says so.
