+apps/examples/mm_uaf_test
+=========================
+
+Trips the heap use-after-free detector on purpose, in each of the shapes it
+is meant to catch, and prints what should have been reported for each one.
+
+Build with CONFIG_EXAMPLES_MM_UAF_TEST=y, which requires CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF.
+Run it from TASH as "uaftest".
+
+Cases
+-----
+
+  1. Write into a chunk which is still on the free list.
+     Reported by DEBUG_MM_UAF on its own.
+
+  2. Write to the first word of a freed block.
+     Inside the free node bookkeeping, so DEBUG_MM_UAF on its own cannot see
+     it. Reported once DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE is enabled, because a held chunk
+     is in no list and its whole payload carries the pattern.
+
+  3. Write after another allocation has taken the block.
+     Needs DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE. Without it the address already belongs to the
+     new owner and no check of the contents can tell the two writers apart.
+
+  4. Free the same block twice.
+     Reported either way, but with DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE the block is still
+     held, so the report names both callers.
+
+  5. Ordinary allocation traffic, which must stay silent. A detector which
+     reports on correct code is worse than no detector, so treat any output
+     during this case as a failure.
+
+The test leaves the heap corrupted on purpose. Reboot the board afterwards,
+and do not enable it in a product build.
